A gas station is selling fuel with the following discount table:

Ethanol:
up to 20 liters, 3% discount per liter;
above 20 liters, 5% discount per liter.

Gasoline:
up to 20 liters, 4% discount per liter;
above 20 liters, 6% discount per liter.

Write a C program that reads the number of liters sold, the type of fuel (coded as follows: A-ethanol, G-gasoline)
calculates and prints the amount to be paid by the customer
knowing that the price of a liter of gasoline is $2.50 and the price of a liter of ethanol is $1.90.

#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
  float litros, preco;
  char combustivel;
  printf("Fuel type (A-Ethanol / G-Gasoline): ");
  scanf(" %c", &combustivel);
  printf("Amount in liters: ");
  scanf("%f", &litros);
  if (combustivel == 'A' || combustivel == 'a'){
    if (litros <= 20) {
      preco = litros * 1.90 * 0.97;
    } else {
      preco = litros * 1.90 * 0.95;
    }
  }
  else if (combustivel == 'G' || combustivel == 'g'){
    if (litros <= 20) {
      preco = 2.50 * litros * 0.96;
    } else { 
      preco = 2.50 * litros * 0.94;
    }
  }
  else {
    printf("Invalid fuel type!");
    return 1;
  }  
   
  printf("The total amount to be paid is $ %.2f", preco);
  return 0;
}
